{"tmdb":1621673,"tagline":"","synopsis":"In 1963, as Japan emerged from the shadows of war into an era of extraordinary transformation, an unlikely song made music history. \"Ue o Muite Arukou,\" known internationally as \"Sukiyaki,\" became the first Japanese song to top the U.S. Billboard charts, remaining at No. 1 for three weeks and captivating listeners around the world.","directors":[{"name":"Takahisa Zeze","id":106549}],"cast":[{"actor":"Junichi Okada","role":"Hachidai Nakamura","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/pk5rltXChl9A3HjS6iQLGt1DWJY.jpg","tmdb":119241},{"actor":"Tori Matsuzaka","role":"Rokusuke Ei","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/8JcMm3al3gySuay2EiW3CI19Apj.jpg","tmdb":1105808},{"actor":"Taiga Nakano","role":"Kyu Sakamoto","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/5mVGPU8dylxs7tnpI2VfeKkumoJ.jpg","tmdb":1328328},{"actor":"Nana Seino","role":"Junko Nakamura","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/nCXAhyUSD5SgXbq3PRTt5oGKuH1.jpg","tmdb":1393772},{"actor":"Mone Kamishiraishi","role":"Alice","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/cPydoy2sSqFDsbXeBPmzQGPmq0R.jpg","tmdb":1369100},{"actor":"Riisa Naka","role":"Masako Ei","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tqFHQiJUycuob3ytvilaAWDlbQ8.jpg","tmdb":122468},{"actor":"Tao Tsuchiya","role":"Yukiko Kashiwagi","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/n2665l3bguzDTm5CnyP99ipU9Z0.jpg","tmdb":1076363},{"actor":"Riho Yoshioka","role":"Tetsuko Kuroyanagi","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/b8DoAyEouFQJt15EtAl9ASKiJP9.jpg","tmdb":1576235},{"actor":"Tomoya Maeno","role":"Kiyoshi Atsumi","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/uIJtJ78kXi323Wub37iklyuyseJ.jpg","tmdb":509439},{"actor":"Kogaken","role":"Norihei Miki","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/nXyC29RfFXReluY05UMIpW8UL2J.jpg","tmdb":5090700},{"actor":"Hiroko Yakushimaru","role":"Iku Ooshima","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qfBiEx267wNsimyHX4BDeTc94Hk.jpg","tmdb":118407},{"actor":"Hiroshi Abe","role":"Producer Nabeyama","phot